[{:db/id 17592186172067 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6027249a-4549-596f-8431-62871ac4f14f" "question-5c7770c4-cc2d-59e3-b961-52e126102cc7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171873 :question/problem "Compute $\\textrm E[5X-2Y]$ if $\\textrm E[X]=1$ and $\\textrm E[Y] = 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For any random variables $X,Y$ and any constants $a,b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[aX+bY] = a \\textrm E[X] + b \\textrm E[Y].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[5X-2Y] & =5\\text{E}[X]-2\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =5(1)-2(2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172069 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bb9379fc-94d7-554c-91be-7390d9b4d8c5" "question-1c83b6b2-8cdb-5214-8b06-fddb32644de4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171875 :question/problem "Andrea has two dice. One of them is fair, and the other is not. The rolls of the unfair die follow the probability mass function $f(y)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected sum of the outcomes of $2$ throws of the fair die and $4$ throws of the unfair one?\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Let $X_i$ be the $i$th score obtained from the fair die, and let $Y_j$ be the $j$th score obtained from the unfair die. Also, let $X$ and $Y$ represent the scores obtained from a typical throw of the fair and unfair die, respectively.\n\nThen, we need to calculate \n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\left[\n\\sum_{i=1}^2 X_i + \\sum_{j=1}^4 Y_j\n\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of expected value, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{X}_{i}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{4}{Y}_{j}] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}\\text{E}[{X}_{i}]+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{4}\\text{E}[{Y}_{j}] \\\\  & =2\\text{E}[X]+4\\text{E}[Y],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the last equality above is true because $\\textrm E[X_i] = \\textrm E[X]$ and $\\textrm E[Y_j] = \\textrm E[Y]$ for all $1\\leq i \\leq 2,\\: 1\\leq j\\leq 4.$\n\nThe expected values of $X$ and $Y$ are calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+5\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}+5\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}=\\frac{13}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[2X+4Y]=2\\textrm E[X]+4\\textrm E[Y]= 2\\cdot \\dfrac{7}{2}+4\\cdot \\dfrac{13}{4} =20.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172068 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-71672eae-2331-5c0a-933f-85ee828fb39f" "question-f7e9fbd8-7003-5d39-9b68-8eea275c407a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171874 :question/problem "The probability distributions of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{1}{6}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{1}{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{1}{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{1}{6}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{1}{2}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nFind $\\textrm E[XY].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X\\cdot Y]=\\textrm E[X]\\cdot \\textrm E[Y].\n$$\n\nThe expected values of $X$ and $Y$ are calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}=0 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X\\cdot Y] = \\textrm E[X] \\cdot \\textrm E[Y] = 0  \\cdot \\dfrac{9}{4} = 0.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-6027249a-4549-596f-8431-62871ac4f14f" :question/id #uuid "6027249a-4549-596f-8431-62871ac4f14f" :question/math-academy-id "q-84119" :question/problem "Compute $\\text{E}[6X-4Z]$ if $\\text{E}[X]=2$ and $\\text{E}[Z]=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[6X-4Z] & =6\\text{E}[X]-4\\text{E}[Z] \\\\  & =6(2)-4(2) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d34edc72-08f2-5a09-a869-52843437095c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d34edc72-08f2-5a09-a869-52843437095c" :answer-field/id #uuid "d34edc72-08f2-5a09-a869-52843437095c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-17daf1a4-33c1-5939-b054-77beedb8860e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c7814c79-cfcb-5c83-9048-4de44313b52b" "answer-f708cd44-8be3-544d-92b7-25ad677ca00a" "answer-661aba9a-91d3-550a-ba62-78837217c25f" "answer-17daf1a4-33c1-5939-b054-77beedb8860e" "answer-16cf25d3-3fb6-57df-8d11-0f924a53ee27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7814c79-cfcb-5c83-9048-4de44313b52b" :answer/id #uuid "c7814c79-cfcb-5c83-9048-4de44313b52b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f708cd44-8be3-544d-92b7-25ad677ca00a" :answer/id #uuid "f708cd44-8be3-544d-92b7-25ad677ca00a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-661aba9a-91d3-550a-ba62-78837217c25f" :answer/id #uuid "661aba9a-91d3-550a-ba62-78837217c25f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17daf1a4-33c1-5939-b054-77beedb8860e" :answer/id #uuid "17daf1a4-33c1-5939-b054-77beedb8860e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16cf25d3-3fb6-57df-8d11-0f924a53ee27" :answer/id #uuid "16cf25d3-3fb6-57df-8d11-0f924a53ee27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5c7770c4-cc2d-59e3-b961-52e126102cc7" :question/id #uuid "5c7770c4-cc2d-59e3-b961-52e126102cc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-84114" :question/problem "Compute $\\text{E}[2A+5B]$ if $\\text{E}[A]=-0.5$ and $\\text{E}[B]=0.4.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2A+5B] & =2\\text{E}[A]+5\\text{E}[B] \\\\  & =2(-0.5)+5(0.4) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2e370811-e954-52e3-b140-bd302be817ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2e370811-e954-52e3-b140-bd302be817ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e370811-e954-52e3-b140-bd302be817ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c70b5ffd-7119-5ff8-9daa-256ffcaa4efe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a214745e-25b5-5f2d-a91a-d1c90719a886" "answer-d9c27718-c436-51fd-b9f5-723bbf094324" "answer-c70b5ffd-7119-5ff8-9daa-256ffcaa4efe" "answer-808a6aa2-08e3-58bf-aea1-5157e9a25005" "answer-790957d5-7b02-5a48-b8e5-2947b0bb92f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a214745e-25b5-5f2d-a91a-d1c90719a886" :answer/id #uuid "a214745e-25b5-5f2d-a91a-d1c90719a886" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9c27718-c436-51fd-b9f5-723bbf094324" :answer/id #uuid "d9c27718-c436-51fd-b9f5-723bbf094324" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c70b5ffd-7119-5ff8-9daa-256ffcaa4efe" :answer/id #uuid "c70b5ffd-7119-5ff8-9daa-256ffcaa4efe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-808a6aa2-08e3-58bf-aea1-5157e9a25005" :answer/id #uuid "808a6aa2-08e3-58bf-aea1-5157e9a25005" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-790957d5-7b02-5a48-b8e5-2947b0bb92f4" :answer/id #uuid "790957d5-7b02-5a48-b8e5-2947b0bb92f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bb9379fc-94d7-554c-91be-7390d9b4d8c5" :question/id #uuid "bb9379fc-94d7-554c-91be-7390d9b4d8c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-127990" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ represents the age of a randomly selected child from a football team, and the random variable $Y$  represents the age of a randomly selected child from a baseball team. The probability distributions of $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$13$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.55$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nOne child is selected at random from each team. Calculate the expected sum of ages of the two children." :question/worked-solution "We need to calculate $\\text{E}[X+Y].$\n\nRecall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nThe expected values of $X$ and $Y$ are calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =10\\cdot 0.1+11\\cdot 0.2+12\\cdot 0.35+13\\cdot 0.35=11.95 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & =10\\cdot 0.2+11\\cdot 0.25+12\\cdot 0.55=11.35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X+Y]=\\text{E}[X]+\\text{E}[Y]=11.95+11.35=23.3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d3dc5651-5264-5a29-88a8-48b8aceed863"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d3dc5651-5264-5a29-88a8-48b8aceed863" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3dc5651-5264-5a29-88a8-48b8aceed863" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-421fad1d-d69f-5891-8cc7-ecd706d5a9a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a62fad79-f235-53ed-b675-fb289b67841d" "answer-421fad1d-d69f-5891-8cc7-ecd706d5a9a6" "answer-d7d51d80-2bc7-55bc-b601-dd519fcc0b6f" "answer-ba9be5c1-e0d2-5c75-8629-59c132cf1df6" "answer-5dcc713b-da30-5b10-aa86-0d87c3de5ade"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a62fad79-f235-53ed-b675-fb289b67841d" :answer/id #uuid "a62fad79-f235-53ed-b675-fb289b67841d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-421fad1d-d69f-5891-8cc7-ecd706d5a9a6" :answer/id #uuid "421fad1d-d69f-5891-8cc7-ecd706d5a9a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7d51d80-2bc7-55bc-b601-dd519fcc0b6f" :answer/id #uuid "d7d51d80-2bc7-55bc-b601-dd519fcc0b6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba9be5c1-e0d2-5c75-8629-59c132cf1df6" :answer/id #uuid "ba9be5c1-e0d2-5c75-8629-59c132cf1df6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5dcc713b-da30-5b10-aa86-0d87c3de5ade" :answer/id #uuid "5dcc713b-da30-5b10-aa86-0d87c3de5ade" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1c83b6b2-8cdb-5214-8b06-fddb32644de4" :question/id #uuid "1c83b6b2-8cdb-5214-8b06-fddb32644de4" :question/math-academy-id "q-109523" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ represents the number of foreign ships arriving daily at port $A,$ and the random variable $Y$ is the number of foreign ships arriving daily at port $B.$ The probability distributions of $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nCalculate the expected number of foreign ships arriving at both ports per day." :question/worked-solution "We need to calculate $\\text{E}[X+Y].$\n\nRecall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nThe expected values of $X$ and $Y$ are calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot 0.5+2\\cdot 0.2+3\\cdot 0.2=1.5 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & =0\\cdot 0.5+1\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.2=0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X+Y]=\\text{E}[X]+\\text{E}[Y]=1.5+0.7=2.2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f2c231ef-5289-5db7-b09f-259aa2d1f08e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f2c231ef-5289-5db7-b09f-259aa2d1f08e" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2c231ef-5289-5db7-b09f-259aa2d1f08e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8021804a-9e55-54c7-b163-b44b22a1e15b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3e4416a7-c43c-57eb-a040-a40e34d1544e" "answer-07711760-4d84-5bf1-aeae-3f76e11395e1" "answer-8021804a-9e55-54c7-b163-b44b22a1e15b" "answer-f1ca42e5-2dbc-534c-8efd-87dde32f4b8d" "answer-78ea3679-b1e5-565c-9b6d-5721d6fd07ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e4416a7-c43c-57eb-a040-a40e34d1544e" :answer/id #uuid "3e4416a7-c43c-57eb-a040-a40e34d1544e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07711760-4d84-5bf1-aeae-3f76e11395e1" :answer/id #uuid "07711760-4d84-5bf1-aeae-3f76e11395e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8021804a-9e55-54c7-b163-b44b22a1e15b" :answer/id #uuid "8021804a-9e55-54c7-b163-b44b22a1e15b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1ca42e5-2dbc-534c-8efd-87dde32f4b8d" :answer/id #uuid "f1ca42e5-2dbc-534c-8efd-87dde32f4b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78ea3679-b1e5-565c-9b6d-5721d6fd07ea" :answer/id #uuid "78ea3679-b1e5-565c-9b6d-5721d6fd07ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-71672eae-2331-5c0a-933f-85ee828fb39f" :question/id #uuid "71672eae-2331-5c0a-933f-85ee828fb39f" :question/math-academy-id "q-108557" :question/problem "For the random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{E}[X]=4$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=5.$ Find $\\text{E}[XY].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]\n$$\n\nIn this case, however, we don't know whether $X$ and $Y$ are independent. Therefore, $\\text{E}[XY]$ is impossible to determine using only the given information." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d53ec05-4864-5ee5-aafb-250240dc4a59"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d53ec05-4864-5ee5-aafb-250240dc4a59" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d53ec05-4864-5ee5-aafb-250240dc4a59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-162c5f57-a9f7-53b8-b1b6-a0fc170863c8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cad2f441-85b5-58a5-b9bd-71012fa267c2" "answer-e6e25341-2ac1-5168-8ae7-79e7802ae332" "answer-4ceaed98-0bbd-5176-a144-a357ebbf538f" "answer-621a58ba-7550-520e-a1c2-bd6e7f8b1076" "answer-162c5f57-a9f7-53b8-b1b6-a0fc170863c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cad2f441-85b5-58a5-b9bd-71012fa267c2" :answer/id #uuid "cad2f441-85b5-58a5-b9bd-71012fa267c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6e25341-2ac1-5168-8ae7-79e7802ae332" :answer/id #uuid "e6e25341-2ac1-5168-8ae7-79e7802ae332" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "41" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ceaed98-0bbd-5176-a144-a357ebbf538f" :answer/id #uuid "4ceaed98-0bbd-5176-a144-a357ebbf538f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-621a58ba-7550-520e-a1c2-bd6e7f8b1076" :answer/id #uuid "621a58ba-7550-520e-a1c2-bd6e7f8b1076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-162c5f57-a9f7-53b8-b1b6-a0fc170863c8" :answer/id #uuid "162c5f57-a9f7-53b8-b1b6-a0fc170863c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Impossible to determine from the given information." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f7e9fbd8-7003-5d39-9b68-8eea275c407a" :question/id #uuid "f7e9fbd8-7003-5d39-9b68-8eea275c407a" :question/math-academy-id "q-109349" :question/problem "For the independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{E}[X]=5$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=0.6.$ Find $\\text{E}[XY].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]=5\\cdot 0.6=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e23b2bd8-34af-5d2b-ade2-34acee35a91f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e23b2bd8-34af-5d2b-ade2-34acee35a91f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e23b2bd8-34af-5d2b-ade2-34acee35a91f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a9fd281-dd69-52dc-a834-e9b4ad2064f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c17a86fa-bc5a-5fe9-9dd4-344f750d1934" "answer-6a9fd281-dd69-52dc-a834-e9b4ad2064f2" "answer-0bc88e36-dea8-5f2b-918d-a47448bd8357" "answer-e795fb2f-d97c-5c70-a237-07f228fde701" "answer-7d1be910-5e61-550b-abc3-fe2fa51b8d37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c17a86fa-bc5a-5fe9-9dd4-344f750d1934" :answer/id #uuid "c17a86fa-bc5a-5fe9-9dd4-344f750d1934" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a9fd281-dd69-52dc-a834-e9b4ad2064f2" :answer/id #uuid "6a9fd281-dd69-52dc-a834-e9b4ad2064f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bc88e36-dea8-5f2b-918d-a47448bd8357" :answer/id #uuid "0bc88e36-dea8-5f2b-918d-a47448bd8357" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e795fb2f-d97c-5c70-a237-07f228fde701" :answer/id #uuid "e795fb2f-d97c-5c70-a237-07f228fde701" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d1be910-5e61-550b-abc3-fe2fa51b8d37" :answer/id #uuid "7d1be910-5e61-550b-abc3-fe2fa51b8d37" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Impossible to determine from the given information." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173183 :tutorial/content "We can use the following property to simplify expressions involving expected values:\n\nFor any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[aX+bY] = a \\textrm E[X] + b \\textrm E[Y].\n$$\n\nIn other words, the expected value of a sum of scaled random variables equals the sum of the scaled expected values.\n\nFor example, \n\n$$\n\\textrm E[2X+5Y] = 2 \\textrm E[X] + 5 \\textrm E[Y].\n$$\n\nNote that the property also works with subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[2X-5Y] = 2 \\textrm E[X] - 5 \\textrm E[Y]\n$$\n\nWe can extend this idea to any number of random variables. For example, for any random variables $X_1, X_2,\\ldots, X_n,$ and real constants $a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$, we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[a_1X_1+a_2X_2+\\cdots+ a_nX_n]= a_1\\textrm E[X_1]+a_2\\textrm E[X_2]+\\cdots +a_n\\textrm{E}[X_n],\n$$\n\nor more concisely,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\left[\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i X_i\\right] =\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i \\textrm E[X_i].\n$$\n\nNote that the random variables  $X_1, X_2,\\ldots, X_n,$ are *not* required to be independent." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173187 :tutorial/content "The expected value of the product of two *independent* random variables is equal to the product of the expected values. So, if the random variables $X$ and $Y$ are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X\\cdot Y] = \\textrm E[X]\\cdot \\textrm E[Y].\n$$\n\nFor example, if we know that $X$ are $Y$ are independent, and that $\\textrm E[X]=2$ and $\\textrm E[Y]=3$, then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y] & =\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen working with the expected value of a product of random variables, it's important to check that the variables are independent. The formula above is *not* true if $X$ and $Y$ are not independent.\n\nMore generally, if the random variables $X_1, X_2,\\ldots, X_n$ are *mutually* independent, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X_1\\cdot X_2 \\cdots  X_n]=\\textrm E[X_1]\\cdot \\textrm E[X_2]\\cdot\\ldots\\cdot \\textrm E[X_n],\n$$\n\nor more concisely,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\left[ \\prod_{i=1}^n X_i\\right] = \\prod_{i=1}^n \\textrm E[X_i],\n$$\n\nwhere $\\prod$ is the product operator." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172143 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
